    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe placement decisions here are sound and I want to be clear about that, because the one finding below is narrow. The age-banding logic sits in `Owner` as a `@Transient` derived getter, which matches the established pattern in that class exactly (`getMembershipLevel()`, `getCheckDigit()`, `getIdentityKey()` are all computed-from-own-state derived getters, and `getCheckDigit()` already uses the same \"return `null` to omit the field\" idiom). The mapper's `toAgeBand` expression + default method mirrors the sibling read-only fields (`toContactPreference`, `toLocality`), and keeping the model returning a plain `String` while the mapper bridges to `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum` correctly respects the layering (the `model` package stays free of a `rest.dto` dependency). Logic is in the right unit, nothing is a catch-all, and the schema/OpenAPI additions are consistent across all four dialects.\n\nThe one improvable item:\n\n- `Owner.java:161` references `java.time.Period.between(...)` fully qualified, while `java.time.LocalDate` (same package) is imported at the top of the file and used unqualified throughout. This is an idiom inconsistency a maintainer of this file would clean up. Add `import java.time.Period;` and use `Period.between(...)` to match the surrounding import style.\n\nOne thing I considered and am *not* requesting a change on, for the record: `Owner.getAgeBand()` returns the bare string literals `\"MINOR\"/\"ADULT\"/\"SENIOR\"`, which must stay in lock-step with `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum`'s values (a mismatch would only surface at runtime via `fromValue`). That coupling is real but is the natural consequence of the (correct) layering choice, and introducing a dedicated domain enum just for this would be out of step with the codebase's stringly-typed derived getters (e.g. `toLocality` returning region codes as `String`). So it's acceptable as-is.",
